================================================================================
REACT - CREATING AND SETTING UP A NAVBAR COMPONENT
================================================================================
LESSON OVERVIEW
================================================================================

This lesson covers how to:

- Create a reusable NavBar component
- Organize components inside a components folder
- Import NavBar into App.jsx
- Style the NavBar using Bootstrap
- Create a responsive navigation menu


================================================================================
1. WHAT IS A NAVBAR COMPONENT?
================================================================================

A NavBar is a navigation section usually displayed at the top of a page.

Purpose:
- Navigate between pages or sections
- Display application branding
- Provide navigation links
- Provide buttons or user menu options

Benefits:
- Reusable
- Maintainable
- Organized
- Scalable
- Separates navigation logic from application logic


================================================================================
2. WHY CREATE A SEPARATE NAVBAR COMPONENT?
================================================================================

Without Components:
- All code stays inside App.jsx
- Large files become difficult to maintain
- Code is harder to reuse
- Project structure becomes messy

With Components:
- Features are separated into files
- Components can be reused
- Easier maintenance
- Cleaner project structure
- Easier team collaboration


